%description:

Tcp.prrEnabled:off -- in the recovery, the window is the threshold.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "Proportional Rate Reduction (RFC 6937) during fast recovery instead of
classic cwnd inflation/halving".

The classes: on (true, the default) and off (false, the value of LegacyTcp). The code: at the
start of a recovery, cwnd and ssthresh become the reduced value
(Rfc6675Recovery::step4()); with PRR, Rfc6675Recovery::prrCwndReduction() then sets cwnd to
pipe + sndcnt at each ACK, so the window comes down over the recovery; without PRR, cwnd
stays at ssthresh. PRR needs SACK; without SACK, the class is the same as off. This test separates "off" from "on".

Host under test: host1, which sends 200000 bytes; the round trip is 40 ms, and the tap drops the 30th data segment
once. Observation: level 2, the window does not change in 30 ms after the threshold of the
recovery, which lasts about two round trips.

%# parameter: Tcp.prrEnabled
%# class: off
%# value: false
%# key: *.host1.tcp.prrEnabled
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpPrrEnabledOff")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 + 41992 && ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B").nth(1).drop()
                     .describe("the 30th data segment of host1, the first time"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("ssthresh")
                  .filterValueAtMost(1e8)
                  .captureMax("threshold", "value")
                  .describe("the threshold at the start of the recovery")
                  .within(2.0))
        .never(on("host1.tcp").signal("cwnd")
                   .describe("a change of the window in the recovery")
                   .within(0.03));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpPrrEnabledOff compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.prrEnabled = false    # the parameter under test
*.linkDelay = 10ms
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 200000B
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpPrrEnabledOff: PASS
